 ^STRUCTURE                   = "CHEMIN_MIN.FMT"
DESCRIPTION                   = "This table contains mineral abundances and
 analytical errors derived from diffraction-all K-alpha diffraction data for
 the Ubajara drill sample, analyzed in CheMin cell number 15a (Kapton
 window). The analysis is based on RDA file
 CMB_737119969RDA38251010774CH00111P1. That RDA file represents the first
 night of analysis, with files produced on sol 3825. Warm temperatures
 inside CheMin (up to ~30 degrees centigrade, with correspondingly low
 relative humidity) cause conversion of gypsum to bassanite over time
 (Vaniman et al., 2018, American Mineralogist 103, 1011-1020); analyses of
 Ubajara on four different sols (files produced on sols 3825, 3830, 3833,
 and 3842) showed that starkeyite observed on sol 3825 dehydrated in a
 similar manner, but becoming X-ray amorphous rather than converting to a
 less hydrous crystalline Mg-sulfate. For this reason we used the first
 night of analysis to determine the in-situ abundances of gypsum, bassanite,
 starkeyite, and amorphous material in Ubajara. Mineral identifications,
 abundances and analytical errors for crystalline phases were determined
 using the program JADE. In addition to the crystalline phases, high
 intensity in the low 2-theta region and a broad amorphous hump were modeled
 using FULLPAT to indicate that ~60 +/- 23 weight% of the total sample
 consists of X-ray amorphous material, which includes a significant original
 amount of amorphous magnesium sulfate. Column 1 of the table lists mineral
 identifications, column 2 lists the mineral abundances in weight percent,
 and column 3 indicates the estimated 2-sigma analytical errors."
END_OBJECT                    = SPREADSHEET
END

